Game: Rent Day
Players: 2 to 8

Cards:
  A deck called chance cards, starting in the chance pile:
    | name                           | says                                                                                                       | copies |
    | Advance To Go                  | Their piece moves forward to Go.                                                                           | 1      |
    | Advance To Bell Square         | Their piece moves forward to Bell Square.                                                                  | 1      |
    | Advance To Dock Road           | Their piece moves forward to Dock Road.                                                                    | 1      |
    | Advance To The Nearest Utility | Their piece moves forward to the nearest utility.                                                          | 1      |
    | Advance To The Nearest Station | Their piece moves forward to the nearest station. If someone else owns it, they pay its rent to its owner. | 2      |
    | Bank Pays A Dividend           | They get 50 money.                                                                                         | 1      |
    | Get Out Of Jail Free           | They keep this card in their kept cards.                                                                   | 1      |
    | Go Back Three Spaces           | Their piece moves back 3 spaces.                                                                           | 1      |
    | Go To Jail                     | Their piece goes straight to Jail. They are in jail.                                                       | 1      |
    | General Repairs                | They pay 25 for each of their houses. They pay 100 for each of their hotels.                               | 1      |
    | Speeding Fine                  | They pay 15.                                                                                               | 1      |
    | A Trip To North Station        | Their piece moves forward to North Station.                                                                | 1      |
    | A Walk On The Promenade        | Their piece moves forward to The Promenade.                                                                | 1      |
    | Chair Of The Board             | They pay 50 money to each other player.                                                                    | 1      |
    | Building Loan Matures          | They get 150 money.                                                                                        | 1      |
  A deck called treasury cards, starting in the treasury pile:
    | name                      | says                                                                         | copies |
    | Advance To Go             | Their piece moves forward to Go.                                             | 1      |
    | Bank Error In Your Favour | They get 200 money.                                                          | 1      |
    | Doctor's Fee              | They pay 50.                                                                 | 1      |
    | Sale Of Stock             | They get 50 money.                                                           | 1      |
    | Get Out Of Jail Free      | They keep this card in their kept cards.                                     | 1      |
    | Go To Jail                | Their piece goes straight to Jail. They are in jail.                         | 1      |
    | Opera Night               | They get 50 money from each other player.                                    | 1      |
    | Holiday Fund Matures      | They get 100 money.                                                          | 1      |
    | Tax Refund                | They get 20 money.                                                           | 1      |
    | Life Insurance Matures    | They get 100 money.                                                          | 1      |
    | Hospital Fees             | They pay 100.                                                                | 1      |
    | School Fees               | They pay 50.                                                                 | 1      |
    | Consultancy Fee           | They get 25 money.                                                           | 1      |
    | Street Repairs            | They pay 40 for each of their houses. They pay 115 for each of their hotels. | 1      |
    | Beauty Contest Prize      | They get 10 money.                                                           | 1      |
    | Inheritance               | They get 100 money.                                                          | 1      |

Table:
  The chance pile is a pile in the center that no one can see.
  The treasury pile is a pile in the center that no one can see.
  Each player has a kept cards row that everyone can see.

Board:
  The board is a loop of spaces, starting at Go:
    | space           | kind       | color      | price | house price | rent | 1 house | 2 houses | 3 houses | 4 houses | with hotel | tax |
    | Go              | go         |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Mill Lane       | street     | brown      | 60    | 50          | 2    | 10      | 30       | 90       | 160      | 250        |     |
    | Treasury        | treasury   |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Ferry Row       | street     | brown      | 60    | 50          | 4    | 20      | 60       | 180      | 320      | 450        |     |
    | Income Tax      | tax        |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            | 200 |
    | North Station   | station    |            | 200   |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Ash Street      | street     | light blue | 100   | 50          | 6    | 30      | 90       | 270      | 400      | 550        |     |
    | Chance          | chance     |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Birch Street    | street     | light blue | 100   | 50          | 6    | 30      | 90       | 270      | 400      | 550        |     |
    | Cedar Avenue    | street     | light blue | 120   | 50          | 8    | 40      | 100      | 300      | 450      | 600        |     |
    | Jail            | jail       |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Dock Road       | street     | pink       | 140   | 100         | 10   | 50      | 150      | 450      | 625      | 750        |     |
    | Power Works     | utility    |            | 150   |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Quay Street     | street     | pink       | 140   | 100         | 10   | 50      | 150      | 450      | 625      | 750        |     |
    | Harbour Way     | street     | pink       | 160   | 100         | 12   | 60      | 180      | 500      | 700      | 900        |     |
    | East Station    | station    |            | 200   |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Rose Lane       | street     | orange     | 180   | 100         | 14   | 70      | 200      | 550      | 750      | 950        |     |
    | Treasury        | treasury   |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Lily Lane       | street     | orange     | 180   | 100         | 14   | 70      | 200      | 550      | 750      | 950        |     |
    | Iris Road       | street     | orange     | 200   | 100         | 16   | 80      | 220      | 600      | 800      | 1000       |     |
    | Free Parking    | parking    |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Market Square   | street     | red        | 220   | 150         | 18   | 90      | 250      | 700      | 875      | 1050       |     |
    | Chance          | chance     |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Guild Street    | street     | red        | 220   | 150         | 18   | 90      | 250      | 700      | 875      | 1050       |     |
    | Bell Square     | street     | red        | 240   | 150         | 20   | 100     | 300      | 750      | 925      | 1100       |     |
    | South Station   | station    |            | 200   |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Linden Walk     | street     | yellow     | 260   | 150         | 22   | 110     | 330      | 800      | 975      | 1150       |     |
    | Elm Walk        | street     | yellow     | 260   | 150         | 22   | 110     | 330      | 800      | 975      | 1150       |     |
    | Pump House      | utility    |            | 150   |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Oak Gardens     | street     | yellow     | 280   | 150         | 24   | 120     | 360      | 850      | 1025     | 1200       |     |
    | Go To Jail      | go to jail |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Crown Row       | street     | green      | 300   | 200         | 26   | 130     | 390      | 900      | 1100     | 1275       |     |
    | Bishop's Row    | street     | green      | 300   | 200         | 26   | 130     | 390      | 900      | 1100     | 1275       |     |
    | Treasury        | treasury   |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Castle Row      | street     | green      | 320   | 200         | 28   | 150     | 450      | 1000     | 1200     | 1400       |     |
    | West Station    | station    |            | 200   |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Chance          | chance     |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Harbour Heights | street     | dark blue  | 350   | 200         | 35   | 175     | 500      | 1100     | 1300     | 1500       |     |
    | Luxury Tax      | tax        |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            | 100 |
    | The Promenade   | street     | dark blue  | 400   | 200         | 50   | 200     | 600      | 1400     | 1700     | 2000       |     |
  Each player has a piece that starts on Go.
  Each player has 1500 money that everyone can see.
  Players pay with money.
  There are two six-sided dice.
  Spaces can have houses and a hotel.
  Spaces can be mortgaged.
  The bank has 32 houses and 12 hotels.
  Players can be in jail.
  Players can have jail turns.
  Spaces can be up for auction.
  Players can be bidding.
  Players can be the high bidder.
  The game has a high bid of 0.
  Spaces can be offered.
  Spaces can be asked for.
  Cards can be handed over.
  Cards can be claimed.
  Players can be proposing.
  Players can be the trade partner.
  The game has a cash offer of 0.
  The game has a cash request of 0.

Setup:
  Shuffle the chance pile.
  Shuffle the treasury pile.

Rent:
  A street's rent depends on its houses and hotel.
  A street in a full set with no buildings has double rent.
  A station's rent is 25, 50, 100 or 200 when its owner has 1, 2, 3 or 4 stations.
  A utility's rent is 4 times the roll, or 10 times when its owner has both.
  A mortgaged space's rent is 0.

Phase: playing
  Hint: Roll the dice, then buy, build, or end your turn. A double rolls again.
  Players take turns.
  A player may roll the dice.
    Only if no player has less than 0 money.
    Only if they are not in jail.
    Only if they have not rolled for a double this turn.
    Only if one of:
      they have not rolled this turn
      they rolled a double
    Only if one of:
      they have not rolled this turn
      it has no price
      someone owns it
      it is up for auction
    Then:
      No space is up for auction.
      Roll the dice.
      If they have rolled fewer than 3 doubles this turn, their piece moves forward by the roll.
  A player may pay to leave jail.
    Only if no player has less than 0 money.
    Only if they are in jail.
    Only if they have not rolled this turn.
    Only if they have at least 50 money.
    Then:
      They pay 50.
      They are not in jail.
      Their jail turns go back to 0.
  A player may roll for a double.
    Only if no player has less than 0 money.
    Only if they are in jail.
    Only if they have not rolled this turn.
    Then:
      Roll the dice.
      If they rolled a double, they are not in jail.
      If they are in jail, they gain 1 jail turn.
      If they are not in jail, their jail turns go back to 0.
      If they are not in jail, their piece moves forward by the roll.
  A player may use a Get Out Of Jail Free.
    Only if no player has less than 0 money.
    Only if they are in jail.
    Only if they have not rolled this turn.
    Only if their kept cards has a Get Out Of Jail Free.
    Then:
      They are not in jail.
      Their jail turns go back to 0.
      A Get Out Of Jail Free from their kept cards goes to the bottom of the pile it came from.
  A player may buy the space they are on.
    Only if no player has less than 0 money.
    Only if they have rolled this turn.
    Only if it has a price.
    Only if no one owns it.
    Only if it is not up for auction.
    Only if they have at least its price in money.
    Then:
      They pay its price.
      They own it.
  A player may auction the space they are on.
    Only if no player has less than 0 money.
    Only if they have rolled this turn.
    Only if it has a price.
    Only if no one owns it.
    Only if it is not up for auction.
    Then:
      It is up for auction.
      Every player is bidding.
      The high bid is 0.
      The auction phase starts with the player on their left.
  A player may build a house on a street they own.
    Only if no player has less than 0 money.
    Only if they own every street of its color.
    Only if it has no hotel.
    Only if no street of its color has fewer buildings.
    Only if no street of its color is mortgaged.
    Only if they have at least its house price in money.
    Only if one of:
      it has fewer than 4 houses
      the bank has a hotel
    Only if one of:
      it has 4 houses
      the bank has a house
    Then:
      They pay its house price.
      If it has 4 houses, it gets a hotel from the bank.
      If it has a hotel, its houses go back to the bank.
      If it has no hotel, it gets a house from the bank.
  A player may trade with another player.
    Only if no player has less than 0 money.
    Then:
      They are proposing.
      That player is the trade partner.
      The cash offer is 0.
      The cash request is 0.
      The trade phase starts with them.
  A player may end their turn.
    Only if no player has less than 0 money.
    Only if they have rolled this turn.
    Only if one of:
      they did not roll a double
      they are in jail
      they have rolled for a double this turn
    Only if one of:
      it has no price
      someone owns it
      it is up for auction
    Then:
      No space is up for auction.
  Any player may take a mortgage on a space they own.
    Only if it is not mortgaged.
    Only if no street of its color has a building.
    Then:
      They get 50% of its price.
      It is mortgaged.
  Any player may pay off a mortgage on a space they own.
    Only if it is mortgaged.
    Only if they have at least 55% of its price in money.
    Then:
      They pay 55% of its price.
      It is not mortgaged.
  Any player may sell a house on a street they own.
    Only if one of:
      it has a house
      it has a hotel
    Only if no street of its color has more buildings.
    Only if one of:
      it has no hotel
      the bank has at least 4 houses
    Then:
      They get 50% of its house price.
      If it has no hotel, one of its houses goes back to the bank.
      If it has a hotel, it gets 4 houses from the bank.
      If it has a hotel, its hotel goes back to the bank.
  Any player may give up.
    Only if they have less than 0 money.
    Then:
      Their houses go back to the bank.
      Their hotels go back to the bank.
      If they owe the bank, their spaces are no longer mortgaged.
      Everything they own goes to the player they owe.
      They are out.
  When a player has rolled 3 doubles this turn:
    Only if they are not in jail.
    Their piece goes straight to Jail.
    They are in jail.
  When a player lands on a go to jail space:
    Their piece goes straight to Jail.
    They are in jail.
  When a player has 3 jail turns:
    They pay 50.
    They are not in jail.
    Their jail turns go back to 0.
    Their piece moves forward by the roll.
  When a piece passes Go:
    Its player gets 200 money.
  When a player lands on a space someone else owns:
    They pay its rent to its owner.
  When a player lands on a tax space:
    They pay its tax.
  When a player lands on a chance space:
    They draw from the chance pile and do what it says.
  When a player lands on a treasury space:
    They draw from the treasury pile and do what it says.
  After a player ends their turn, the turn passes to the left.

Phase: auction
  Hint: Bid more than the high bid, or drop out.
  A player may bid an amount.
    Only if they are bidding.
    Only if the amount is more than the high bid.
    Only if they have at least the amount in money.
    Then:
      The high bid is the amount.
      No player is the high bidder.
      They are the high bidder.
  A player may drop out.
    Only if they are bidding.
    Only if they are not the high bidder.
    Then:
      They are not bidding.
  When a player is the high bidder:
    Only if no other player is bidding.
    They pay the high bid.
    They own the space that is up for auction.
    They are not the high bidder.
    They are not bidding.
    The space that is up for auction is not up for auction.
    The high bid is 0.
    Go back to the interrupted turn.
  When no player is bidding:
    The high bid is 0.
    Go back to the interrupted turn.
  After a player bids or drops out, the turn passes to the next player on the left who is bidding.

Phase: trade
  Hint: Offer and ask for spaces, cash and kept cards, then propose. The other player accepts or declines.
  A player may offer a space they own.
    Only if they are proposing.
    Only if it is not offered.
    Only if no street of its color has a building.
    Then:
      It is offered.
  A player may ask for a space the trade partner owns.
    Only if they are proposing.
    Only if it is not asked for.
    Only if no street of its color has a building.
    Then:
      It is asked for.
  A player may offer to pay an amount.
    Only if they are proposing.
    Only if they have at least the amount in money.
    Then:
      The cash offer is the amount.
  A player may ask to be paid an amount.
    Only if they are proposing.
    Then:
      The cash request is the amount.
  A player may offer everything they keep.
    Only if they are proposing.
    Only if their kept cards are not empty.
    Then:
      Every card in their kept cards is handed over.
  A player may ask for everything the trade partner keeps.
    Only if they are proposing.
    Then:
      For the trade partner, every card in their kept cards is claimed.
  A player may propose the trade.
    Only if they are proposing.
    Only if one of:
      some space is offered
      some space is asked for
      some card is handed over
      some card is claimed
      the cash offer is more than 0
      the cash request is more than 0
  A player may cancel the trade.
    Only if they are proposing.
    Then:
      No space is offered.
      No space is asked for.
      No card is handed over.
      No card is claimed.
      No player is proposing.
      No player is the trade partner.
      The cash offer is 0.
      The cash request is 0.
      Go back to the interrupted turn.
  A player may accept the trade.
    Only if they are the trade partner.
    Only if they have at least the cash request in money.
    Then:
      They own every space that is offered.
      Every card that is handed over goes to their kept cards.
      They pay the cash request to the player who is proposing.
      For the player who is proposing, they own every space that is asked for.
      For the player who is proposing, every card that is claimed goes to their kept cards.
      For the player who is proposing, they pay the cash offer to the trade partner.
      No space is offered.
      No space is asked for.
      No card is handed over.
      No card is claimed.
      No player is proposing.
      No player is the trade partner.
      The cash offer is 0.
      The cash request is 0.
      Go back to the interrupted turn.
  A player may decline the trade.
    Only if they are the trade partner.
    Then:
      No space is offered.
      No space is asked for.
      No card is handed over.
      No card is claimed.
      No player is proposing.
      No player is the trade partner.
      The cash offer is 0.
      The cash request is 0.
      Go back to the interrupted turn.
  After a player proposes the trade, the turn passes to the next player on the left who is the trade partner.

End:
  The game ends when one player is left.
  That player wins.

Example: landing on someone else's street pays them rent
  Given p1 owns Rose Lane
  And p0 is on Cedar Avenue
  And the next roll is 3 and 4
  When p0 rolls the dice
  Then p0 is on Rose Lane
  And p0 has 1486 money
  And p1 has 1514 money

Example: a player can buy the street they land on
  Given p0 is on Cedar Avenue
  And the next roll is 3 and 4
  When p0 rolls the dice
  And p0 buys the space they are on
  Then it is accepted
  And p0 owns Rose Lane
  And p0 has 1320 money

Example: you cannot buy before rolling
  Given p0 is on Rose Lane
  When p0 buys the space they are on
  Then it is rejected because "they have rolled this turn"

Example: you cannot buy a space that has no price
  Given the chance pile has a Building Loan Matures
  And p0 is on Go
  And the next roll is 3 and 4
  When p0 rolls the dice
  And p0 buys the space they are on
  Then it is rejected because "it has a price"

Example: you cannot buy a space someone owns
  Given p1 owns Rose Lane
  And p0 is on Cedar Avenue
  And the next roll is 3 and 4
  When p0 rolls the dice
  And p0 buys the space they are on
  Then it is rejected because "no one owns it"

Example: you cannot buy without enough money
  Given p0 has 100 money
  And p0 is on Cedar Avenue
  And the next roll is 3 and 4
  When p0 rolls the dice
  And p0 buys the space they are on
  Then it is rejected because "they have at least its price in money"

Example: you cannot roll twice in one turn
  Given p0 is on Go
  And the next roll is 1 and 2
  When p0 rolls the dice
  And p0 rolls the dice
  Then it is rejected because "they have not rolled this turn or they rolled a double"

Example: you cannot end your turn before rolling
  When p0 ends their turn
  Then it is rejected because "they have rolled this turn"

